       892           ******************************************************************                                              
       893           *****                                                        *****                                              
       894           ***** 8000-CHECK-DB2-CONNECTION MUST BE PERFORMED EACH AND   *****                                              
       895           ***** EVERYTIME A DB2 PROGRAM IS ENTERED OR EXECUTED, AND IT *****                                              
       896           ***** MUST BE BEFORE THE FIRST SQL STATEMENT IN THE PROGRAM  *****                                              
       897           ***** EXECUTED.                                              *****                                              
       898           *****                                                        *****                                              
       899           ******************************************************************                                              
       900                                                                                                                           
       901           *8000-CHECK-DB2-CONNECTION.                                                                                     
       902                                                                                                                           
       903                EXEC SQL                                                                                                   
       904                     INCLUDE DB85102L                                                                                      
       905                END-EXEC.                                                                                                  
       906                                                                                                                           
       907           *****************************************************************                                               
       908           *    DB85102L.  BEGINNING OF INCLUDE COPYBOOK MEMBER DB85102L.  *                                               
       909           *****************************************************************                                               
       910                                                                                                                           
       911            8000-CHECK-DB2-CONNECTION.                                                                                     
       912                                                                                                                           
       913           *****************************************************************                                               
       914           *    8000-CHECK-DB2-CONNECTION MUST BE PERFORMED EACH AND       *                                               
       915           *    EVERYTIME A DB2 PROGRAM IS ENTERED OR EXECUTED, AND IT     *                                               
       916           *    MUST BE BEFORE THE FIRST SQL STATEMENT IN THE PROGRAM GETS *                                               
       917           *    EXECUTED.                                                  *                                               
       918           *****************************************************************                                               
       919                                                                                                                           
       920           *****************************************************************                                               
       921           *    THIS PARAGRAPH BASICALLY DOES THE FOLLOWING:               *                                               
       922           *                                                               *                                               
       923           *    RESET THE STATUS-MAP TO INDICATE A GOOD EXECUTION.         *                                               
       924           *    CHECK TO SEE IF THE CURRENTLY-SET COLLECTION-ID IS THE ONE *                                               
       925           *    WE NEED TO USE FOR THIS PROGRAM.  IF SO, BYPASS EVERYTHING *                                               
       926           *    ELSE.  BUT IF NOT, BUILD AND SET THE COLLECTION-ID IN DB2  *                                               
       927           *    TO THE CORRECT ONE FOR THIS PROGRAM.  ALSO, IF THE PROGRAM *                                               
       928           *    WASN'T PREVIOUSLY CONNECTED TO DB2, READ THE DB2 CLONE     *                                               
1DB2 SQL PRECOMPILER         VERSION 12 REL. 1.0                                                       PAGE 18                       
0      929           *    NUMBER BEFORE SETTING THE COLLECTION-ID, THEN AFTER SETTING*                                               
       930           *    IT (WHICH AUTOMATICALLY PERFORMS THE CONNECT TO DB2),      *                                               
       931           *    RETRIEVE THE SERVER NAME, USER ID AND SQLID FROM DB2.      *                                               
       932           *    ANYWHERE ALONG THE WAY, IF ANY STEP GETS A BAD RETURN CODE,*                                               
       933           *    THEN SET A FLAG FOR THE FAILING STEP IN THE STATUS-MAP,    *                                               
       934           *    BYPASS ALL THE REMAINING STEPS AND EXIT THE PARAGRAPH.     *                                               
       935           *                                                               *                                               
       936           *    NOTE:                                                      *                                               
       937           *        THE 8-CHAR COLLECTION-ID IS MADE UP OF THE FOLLOWING:  *                                               
       938           *        THE PROGRAM'S 7-CHAR COLLECTION-ID-BASE CONSTANT AND   *                                               
       939           *        THE 1-CHAR DB2CLONE NUMBER READ FROM THE FLAT-FILE.    *                                               
       940           *****************************************************************                                               
       941           *    DISPLAY '8000-CHECK-DB2-CONNECTION'                                                                        
       942                MOVE '00000'             TO  DB85102D-CONNECT-STATUS-MAP                                                   
       943                EXEC SQL                                                                                                   
       944                   SET :DB85102D-CURR-COLL-ID = CURRENT PACKAGESET                                                         
       945                END-EXEC                                                                                                   
       946                IF SQLCODE NOT = ZERO                                                                                      
       947                   MOVE '2'  TO  DB85102D-CONNECT-STATUS-MAP(2:1)                                                          
       948                   DISPLAY '  DB85102L RECEIVED NON-ZERO SQLCODE '                                                         
       949                           'TRYING TO RETRIEVE COLLECTION-ID '                                                             
       950                           '''' DB85102D-CURR-COLL-ID '''.'                                                                
       951                   DISPLAY ' THE SQLCODE RETURNED WAS : '                                                                  
       952                                SQLCODE                                                                                    
       953                ELSE                                                                                                       
       954                   MOVE DB85102D-CURR-COLL-ID TO DB85102D-PREV-COLL-ID                                                     
       955                   MOVE DB85102D-CURR-COLL-ID TO DB85102D-TEMP-COLL-ID                                                     
       956                END-IF                                                                                                     
       957           *****************************************************************                                               
       958           *    COMPARE THE FIRST 7 CHARACTERS OF THE CURRENT-COLL-ID WITH *                                               
       959           *    THE COLL-ID BASE OF THIS PARTICULAR PROGRAM. IF THEY DON'T *                                               
       960           *    MATCH, THEN EITHER WE AREN'T YET CONNECTED TO DB2 OR WE    *                                               
       961           *    NEED TO SWITCH TO THE CORRECT COLL-ID FOR THIS PROGRAM.    *                                               
       962           *    IF THEY DO MATCH, THEN WE CAN BYPASS EVERYTHING ELSE.      *                                               
       963           *****************************************************************                                               
       964                IF DB85102D-CURR-COLL-ID (1:7) NOT =                                                                       
       965                                              300-THIS-PGM-DB2-COLL-ID-BASE                                                
       966           *****************************************************************                                               
       967           *        IF NOT YET CONNECTED TO DB2, THEN READ THE DB2 CLONE   *                                               
       968           *        NUMBER FROM THE FLAT FILE AND PLUG IT INTO THE 8TH     *                                               
       969           *        POSITION OF THE COLLECTION-ID.                         *                                               
       970           *****************************************************************                                               
       971                    IF DB85102D-CURR-COLL-ID  = SPACES  OR  LOW-VALUES                                                     
       972                        MOVE SPACES                TO  DB85102D-TEMP-COLL-ID                                               
       973                                                                                                                           
       974                        OPEN INPUT DB2CLONE-FILE                                                                           
       975                        IF 88-DB85102D-DB2CLONE-IO-GOOD                                                                    
       976                           READ DB2CLONE-FILE                                03069799                                      
       977                              INTO DB85102D-DB2CLONE-REC                                                                   
       978                           END-READ                                          03069799                                      
       979                           IF 88-DB85102D-DB2CLONE-IO-GOOD                                                                 
       980                              MOVE DB85102D-DB2-CLONE-NUM  TO                                                              
       981                                          DB85102D-TEMP-COLL-ID (8:3)                                                      
       982                              DISPLAY 'DB85102D-DB2-CLONE-NUM = '                                                          
       983                                       DB85102D-DB2-CLONE-NUM                                                              
       984                           ELSE                                                 03100                                      
       985                              MOVE '1'  TO  DB85102D-CONNECT-STATUS-MAP(1:1)                                               
       986                           END-IF                                               03170                                      
1DB2 SQL PRECOMPILER         VERSION 12 REL. 1.0                                                       PAGE 19                       
0      987                        ELSE                                                                                               
       988                           MOVE '1'  TO  DB85102D-CONNECT-STATUS-MAP(1:1)                                                  
       989                        END-IF                                                                                             
       990                        CLOSE DB2CLONE-FILE                                  06200099                                      
       991                        IF DB85102D-CONNECT-STATUS-MAP(1:1) = '1'                                                          
       992                            GO TO 8000-CHECK-DB2-EXIT                                                                      
       993                        END-IF                                                                                             
       994                    END-IF                                                                                                 
       995                                                                                                                           
       996           *****************************************************************                                               
       997           *        FINISH BUILDING THE COLLECTION-ID BY PLUGGING THE      *                                               
       998           *        PROGRAM'S COLL-ID-BASE INTO THE FIRST 7 POSITIONS. THEN*                                               
       999           *        SET THE COLLECTION-ID IN DB2 BY DOING A "SET CURRENT   *                                               
      1000           *        PACKAGESET" STATEMENT. (NOTE: THIS STATEMENT WILL ALSO *                                               
      1001           *        CAUSE THE IMPLICIT CAF CONNECTION TO DB2 TO OCCUR.)    *                                               
      1002           *****************************************************************                                               
      1003                    MOVE 300-THIS-PGM-DB2-COLL-ID-BASE   TO                                                                
      1004                                                DB85102D-TEMP-COLL-ID (1:7)                                                
      1005                    EXEC SQL                                                                                               
      1006                      SET CURRENT PACKAGESET  = :DB85102D-TEMP-COLL-ID                                                     
      1007                    END-EXEC                                                                                               
      1008                    IF SQLCODE NOT = ZERO                                                                                  
      1009                      MOVE '1'  TO  DB85102D-CONNECT-STATUS-MAP(2:1)                                                       
      1010                      DISPLAY '  DB85102L RECEIVED NON-ZERO SQLCODE '                                                      
      1011                              'TRYING TO SET COLLECTION-ID TO '                                                            
      1012                              '''' DB85102D-TEMP-COLL-ID '''.'                                                             
      1013                      DISPLAY ' THE SQLCODE RETURNED WAS : '                                                               
      1014                                   SQLCODE                                                                                 
      1015                    ELSE                                                                                                   
      1016                      MOVE DB85102D-TEMP-COLL-ID  TO DB85102D-CURR-COLL-ID                                                 
      1017           *****************************************************************                                               
      1018           *          IF DB2 WAS JUST CONNECTED TO FOR THE FIRST TIME,     *                                               
      1019           *          RETRIEVE SOME OF THE CONNECTION INFO FOR FUTURE      *                                               
      1020           *          REFERENCE.                                           *                                               
      1021           *****************************************************************                                               
      1022                      IF DB85102D-PREV-COLL-ID  = SPACES  OR  LOW-VALUES                                                   
      1023                        EXEC SQL                                                                                           
      1024                          SET :DB85102D-DB2-CURR-SERVER = CURRENT SERVER                                                   
      1025                        END-EXEC                                                                                           
      1026                        IF SQLCODE NOT = ZERO                                                                              
      1027                          MOVE '1' TO DB85102D-CONNECT-STATUS-MAP(3:1)                                                     
      1028                          DISPLAY '  DB85102L RECEIVED NON-ZERO SQLCODE '                                                  
      1029                                  'TRYING TO RETRIEVE THE DB2 CURRENT '                                                    
      1030                                  'SERVER.'                                                                                
      1031                          DISPLAY '    THE CURRENT COLLECTION-ID WAS '                                                     
      1032                                  '''' DB85102D-CURR-COLL-ID '''.'                                                         
      1033                          DISPLAY ' THE SQLCODE RETURNED WAS : '                                                           
      1034                                       SQLCODE                                                                             
      1035                        ELSE                                                                                               
      1036                          EXEC SQL                                                                                         
      1037                            SET :DB85102D-DB2-USER  = USER                                                                 
      1038                          END-EXEC                                                                                         
      1039                          IF SQLCODE NOT = ZERO                                                                            
      1040                            MOVE '1'  TO  DB85102D-CONNECT-STATUS-MAP(4:1)                                                 
      1041                          ELSE                                                                                             
      1042                            EXEC SQL                                                                                       
      1043                              SET :DB85102D-DB2-CURR-SQLID  = CURRENT SQLID                                                
